WEBVTT

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.980
Magical Girl Barber Scissors Abby.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.740
M-Magical Girl?

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.170
What is this?

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.850
A magical cube?

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.210
The source of the magic is...

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.780
Over there!

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.700
I know her!

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.520
Asuka-san, um...

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.770
You may laugh if I say this, but...

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.850
When I was a kid,

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.170
my dream was to be a Magical Girl.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:56.890
A Magical Girl who used magic to defeat
the bad guys and save everybody.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.660
I knew it, I just didn't want to admit it.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.880
I can't protect anything.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.120
Don't say that, please.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.670
Kurumi...

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.750
If it weren't for you,

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.220
both Nozomi-san
and I would've been killed.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.010
You saved us!

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.730
Magical Girl Rapture Asuka saved us!

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.180
So...

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.890
I want you to keep your head up and fight,

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.400
and know that the path
you chose was the right one.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.970
But I can't.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:29.690
You can!

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.300
I became a Magical Girl
because I wanted to be like you.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.280
Thank you, Kurumi.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.830
It hurts to have someone
you know get caught up in this.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.170
But the truth of the matter is, right now,

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.880
the only way to win a magical
fight is to use Magical Girls.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.780
It's pathetic.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:04.810
Iizuka-san...

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:09.900
You have things only you can do.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.570
Of course,

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.460
we Magical Girls do, too.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.530
I'll join your spec-ops team.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.230
The Magical Girl Operations
Development Unit,

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.290
M Squad.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:02.010
<b>Three Years Earlier</b>

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:07.010
<b>Mt. Aso, Kumamoto Prefecture, Kyushu
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h— Just Before the Final Battle</b>

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:09.990
I can't do this anymore...

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.010
We started our attack,

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:18.440
and now Magdalena and Hildegarde...

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.700
And Crystal and Patricia...

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.780
We lost four people in just a few hours.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:32.400
There was never any way 
I could take Francine's place.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:34.760
So what do we do, then?

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:37.860
Tamara...

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.500
If we don't fight,

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.870
everything will be over for real.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.510
But...

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.510
No "buts," Rapture!

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.040
Hang in there for just one more hour.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:57.940
One hour...

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.450
Yeah.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.190
One hour.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.650
Give us the last of your courage.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.200
And when that hour's up?

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.580
We'll figure out something then.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:22.550
One more hour of courage from
you may be enough to save humanity.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:29.550
One... more hour...

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.170
Yeah.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.070
Sorry, girls.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:56.420
I'll hang in there just a little longer.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:05.550
<b>Magical Girl Operations Development Unit</b>

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.600
We're ready for you.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.190
I can go in now, right?

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.060
Of course.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:31.490
<b>Welcome! Otori Asuka-san</b>

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.060
Surprise!

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.080
Welcome to M Squad!

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.490
M Squad's throwing you a welcome party!

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:35.470
Thank you, everyone.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:39.820
We'll treat you to some JGSDF rations.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.180
Combat rations?

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.010
We don't have much of a budget.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.040
And they're expired?

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.620
That's why we're eating them.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:49.410
Why do you sound so proud of that?

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:54.140
I'm getting worried about joining M Squad.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.510
Don't say that...

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.810
Spicy stewed saury, huh?

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.320
It's good.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:10.240
Next up is wiener curry.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.390
The roux is really rich.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:17.320
It's pretty good.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.310
<i>You guys are way too excited.</i>

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:22.530
<i>All you did was heat it up.</i>

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.530
Here, this canned stuff is good.

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:27.470
<i>But...</i>

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:29.410
<i>That's not bad.</i>

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:37.420
You know, we never really
introduced ourselves.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:41.000
Oh, you're right.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.980
You all know me and Asuka-san, I'm sure, so...

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:48.800
First, Master Sergeant Yoshino.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:52.010
He won the Sniper Aggregate International at 
AASAM, an international shooting competition.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:53.370
Shima-san,

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.870
just call me Yoshino,
not Master Sergeant Yoshino,

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.200
when we're in the shop.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.850
Sorry.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.410
I'll be more careful.

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:04.380
And Kaede-san is a biathlon medalist.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.670
And I won the Inter-High
Championship in wrestling.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:12.600
Ise-san was with the JGSDF 1st Airborne,

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:17.450
but he quit to do all kinds of illegal stuff
with a PMC based in the Middle East.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:18.730
Hey!

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.000
A lot of stuff happened,

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:23.720
so he quit the PMC and came
back to the JGSDF.

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:25.950
Those are enough introductions!

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:27.960
It was your idea!

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.410
Anyway, let's move on to the next dish.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.370
I'll chop up the rat snake.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:42.040
<b>Closed for Party</b>

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.070
I'm good.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.480
I've had enough.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:38.850
Don't worry about it! Eat up!

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:40.700
No, I mean...

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:52.010
<b>Moscow, Russia</b>

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:55.840
I can't move too many people.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:09:01.630
We've also gotten word that the JSDF has 
established a powerful magical warfare unit.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:02.820
So be careful.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.650
That's all I have to say about this mission.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.100
Any questions?

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.200
None.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.380
Very good.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.240
Get ready to go, then.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:12.990
Yes, sir.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.160
Everyone is counting on you.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.140
Don't disappoint us.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:18.200
Of course.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.690
For your sister's sake, too.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:35.950
<i>My only sister...</i>

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:38.580
<i>And my only hope.</i>

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.130
Japan, huh?

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:04.040
You know what a Topology Bridge is, right?

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:08.000
Just what the brass have told me.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:12.890
A Topology Bridge is what connects
the human world to other worlds,

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:17.110
such the Spirit World and Disas World.

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:19.740
Currently,

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:22.810
there are only two stable bridges on Earth

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.810
that maintain a constant
connection between worlds.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:29.230
Copenhagen in Denmark and Okinawa in Japan.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:34.150
There are also other bridges
called "Random Bridges".

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:35.290
Chu!

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:36.570
As the name suggests,

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:40.370
these appear at random, connecting the worlds.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:42.340
Of course, humans can't detect them.

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:46.700
But even fairly powerful spirits have
a difficult time detecting them, chu!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.480
I see where this is going.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:51.160
Somebody's going to misuse these, huh?

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:56.160
A Random Bridge has appeared
on the Sarobetsu Plain in Hokkaido.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:59.430
We have information that it's going
to be used for inter-world smuggling.

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:02.890
M Squad is going to head there to observe.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:06.000
You'll be leaving at 1200.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:11.610
A modified Osprey from the 1st Helicopter
 Brigade is already on the way there.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.950
We have new information.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:30.550
The local police have received word
of some suspicious foreigners.

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:32.160
When they responded to the call,

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:35.130
about ten police officers were killed.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.660
How awful.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.500
Who did it?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:43.570
The enemy is likely a new Russian mafia,
 the Oboroten.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:46.790
They're sending M Squad
in against a simple mafia?

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:50.480
According to the last transmission
from one of the murdered officers,

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:54.440
the mafia had a mage with
them who used flame magic.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:55.970
Flame...

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.350
Reminds you of Tamara, huh?

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:01.620
She's an elite soldier
for the Russian Federation.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.060
We're not going to find her here.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.280
Yes, of course.

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:09.500
We're almost there.

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:11.100
After we arrive,

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.840
we'll deploy according to the plan.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:16.010
Eliminate the enemy mage
and the Russian mafia,

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:17.710
then secure the bridge!

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:20.830
There are no ROE for M Squad's
special missions.

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:22.010
Give 'em hell!

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.100
Roger!

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.690
The deal's finished, then.

00:12:43.770 --> 00:12:45.240
Bye-bye!

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:51.060
We get all this, and all we had to give
them was four kidnapped Japanese.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:52.640
What a deal.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.620
It's basically free!

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:55.650
Hurry!

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:58.460
We killed those Japanese cops.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.970
Once the stuff's loaded, we're moving!

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:01.950
Da!

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.350
Nazani,

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:05.170
if the enemy shows up...

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:08.510
I should just kill them
all with my magic, right?

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:12.460
Is it true you can take down a tank unit?

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:14.980
Easily.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.340
We'll be counting on you, then,

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:20.530
my cute little witch.

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:23.280
Leave it to me!

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.090
<i>Mike Leader,</i>

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.400
<i>this is Mike 01.</i>

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:51.220
<i>Over.</i>

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:53.250
This is Mike Leader.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:53.930
Over.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.160
<i>Enemy forces sighted.</i>

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:58.520
<i>Their location matches that from the drone.</i>

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:00.230
This is Mike 04.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:02.060
Target confirmed.

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:02.860
Over.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.940
Random Bridge confirmed, too.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.120
<i>However,</i>

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:08.960
<i>there is no sign of the spirits
or Disas they would be trading with.</i>

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:11.260
So they finished their trade, huh?

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:16.720
Mike Team is to begin the assault when you 
hear the sound of the Osprey's machine guns.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:17.520
Over.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.390
<i>Mike 01, roger.</i>

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:20.290
<i>Over.</i>

00:14:22.430 --> 00:14:23.320
Shit!

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:24.750
What is that?

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:27.140
That's not good!

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:31.730
Shit!

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:34.560
Were they lying when they said the
Japanese army was a bunch of pussies?

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:37.390
Lower machine gun is out of ammo!

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:47.700
Shit!

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:48.790
They've got us surrounded!

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:51.020
They have forces on the ground, too?

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:52.160
How'd they get here so fast?

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.010
Hey!

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:54.120
Do something!

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:03.210
What firepower!

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:14.560
Hey!

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.930
That hurt!

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:23.530
The enemy mage is yours.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:24.850
Roger!

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:26.930
I'll take the offensive.

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:29.110
War Nurse, you focus on defense.

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:29.900
Right.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:41.210
Magic Calorie Roll-Up!

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:43.330
Reactive Magic Shield!

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:50.130
My incendiary shot?!

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.960
Magical Girl Trivia!

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:55.140
The Reactive Magic Shield!

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:58.580
It's a defense spell that
blocks enemy attacks

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.090
with a triple-layer magical shield!

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:02.460
The first layer explodes
in response to impact,

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:05.150
diverting the energy, chu!

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.770
So it wasn't Tamara.

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:11.860
It's just a magical mercenary
who's dependent on her item!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:13.800
<i>Crap!</i>

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.440
<i>I need to secure a way out!</i>

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:23.460
Mike 03 incapacitated!

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.790
<i>Another one of my comrades is going to die.</i>

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:34.960
This is my chance!

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.890
Reactive Magic Shield!

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:39.850
Huh?

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.800
It's working after all!

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:42.650
Go!

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.630
What's wrong?

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:49.570
Asuka-san!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:50.980
Fight!

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:52.980
Protect me!

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.050
Arm...

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:12.300
My arm...

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:13.710
It hurts!

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:15.640
It hurts so much!

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:18.620
Help me!

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.000
Help me, Mommy!

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.310
You killed all those cops,

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:25.330
and now you're crying for your mommy?

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.650
Useless fucking kid...

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:38.880
Lt. Shima!

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:41.350
Are you okay?

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:44.410
I guess I embarrassed myself.

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:46.530
She's not badly hurt.

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:49.010
I think I cracked a bone.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.130
I see.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:52.630
I'm glad.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:53.900
I'll heal you right away!

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:57.560
The Russian mafia's dealt with.

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:58.610
Yeah.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:04.680
Should we kill her, too?

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:08.000
Stop.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.960
She's a prisoner, and a source of information.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:12.070
Kurumi, heal her, too.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:12.770
Okay.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.240
Well, you're right.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:22.290
Looks like the Random Bridge closed, chu!

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.410
A Random Bridge never opens
in the same place twice.

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:33.840
I'll tell the guys at Wakkanai
to keep an eye out,

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.160
but it should be fine.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:38.190
Mission complete.

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:39.880
We're getting out of here.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:47.480
<b>Wakkanai City, Hokkaido</b>

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:57.500
<i>A Disas teleportation drug...</i>

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.860
<i>Not only is there a limit on how
many times you can use it,</i>

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.910
<i>but if a normal person uses it,</i>

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:06.110
<i>they run the risk of liquefying
their organs. But...</i>

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:07.440
Shit!

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:11.250
It's better than being killed back there!

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:14.670
This is Wakkanai, probably.

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:18.310
If I can make it to Russiatown...

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:20.640
I didn't think I'd make it in time.

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:23.520
Instead, you came to me.

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:24.700
You!

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:28.280
I'll have a good present
to give my sister.

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:33.390
The Japanese government doesn't know I'm here.

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:35.020
I can't stay here long.

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:37.040
So I'm going to make it fast.

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:45.570
I'm taking that magic item.

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:50.780
Are you another one of those magical bitches?

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:53.750
I've got nothing left to lose!

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:56.710
A Disas magic item?

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:03.420
You made me use my trump card, you whore!

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:07.370
I'll never go back to being human again!

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:10.650
You've got guts, for a mafioso.

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:19.380
Magical Girl Phoenix Tamara.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.510
Phoenix from the Magical Five?

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:27.740
But Phoenix's specialty
is wide-area attacks, right?

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.550
Which means if I get close, you're mine!

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:34.920
You're right. Wide-area
suppression is my specialty.

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:35.940
But...

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:39.300
I can deal with other situations, too!

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:42.350
That knife's just a toy!

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:50.850
The toughest people are the ones
who've found hope in despair.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.350
You're ready for this, right?

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:57.110
The flames of the Phoenix
are as hot as the sun!

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:00.250
Volshebnyy Ognemet!

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:15.420
I'll let you live.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:17.450
I've got a lot of questions.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:20.470
What's inside this?

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:23.020
When you find out,

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:25.200
you'll regret knowing.

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:30.450
A new world order...

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:34.550
Humanity's last war...

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:37.580
The Babel Brigade...

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:53.910
<b>Naha City, Okinawa Prefecture</b>

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:00.980
Leyla?

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:02.790
Giess,

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:05.340
the brigade commander gave
us some stuff to look over.

00:22:11.510 --> 00:22:13.010
Take care of that girl.

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:16.200
You're not going to help me?

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:19.360
I've got preparations to make in Russia.

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:21.910
Not that I care,

00:22:21.910 --> 00:22:24.960
but Giess, doesn't that
outfit make you stand out?

00:22:26.100 --> 00:22:28.230
Just like the Magical Girls,

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:31.170
I use my magic to divert people's attention.

00:22:31.170 --> 00:22:32.320
It's fine.

00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:33.530
I see.

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:39.740
Are you happy?

00:24:12.320 --> 00:24:14.310
Nazani, the girl we captured this episode!

00:24:14.310 --> 00:24:17.180
We'll just have to ask her body
if she knows anything!

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:18.250
You can do it, Kurumi!

00:24:18.250 --> 00:24:20.900
And it's a second swimsuit
episode in Okinawa!

00:24:20.900 --> 00:24:21.860
Heck yeah, chu!

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:22.530
Next time:

00:24:22.140 --> 00:24:25.190
<b>You'll Surely Be a Wonderful Magical Girl</b>

00:24:22.530 --> 00:24:24.380
"You'll Surely Be a Wonderful Magical Girl."

00:24:24.380 --> 00:24:26.810
I feel a new threat approaching, chu!
